{"duration_api_ms":39503,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"8eb9e8e2-1578-441a-bb9c-eca05f774e12","total_cost_usd":0.15462320000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23974,"cache_read_input_tokens":29896,"output_tokens":4054,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1128},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23974,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1488,"cache_read_input_tokens":25574,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2722},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":12135,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0122,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":4054,"cacheReadInputTokens":29896,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23974,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1424232,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1128,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"Every sudo command run on node1 is logged with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"sudo's syslog facility was redirected to local2 via /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog (validated with visudo -c), and /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf routes local2.* to /var/log/sudo-commands.log. Both pre-restart (cmd-de982eebfdc7442e) and post-restart (cmd-d74769a8554842a3) tail outputs show entries with timestamp, user (antrieb), target user, and command, e.g. 'Sep 4 23:56:51 node1 sudo: antrieb : ... USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/id'.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b63497ca083a4e3d\",\"cmd-71ccab3539844e9c\",\"cmd-de982eebfdc7442e\",\"cmd-d74769a8554842a3\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log (auth.log/syslog)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"The rsyslog rule uses a 'stop' directive after routing local2.* to the dedicated file, preventing it from also matching the catch-all *.* rule that feeds /var/log/syslog. Evidence from both before and after the restart (cmd-de982eebfdc7442e, cmd-d74769a8554842a3) shows auth.log and syslog tails contain no COMMAND= lines for the same test sudo invocations, only generic PAM session open/close lines (which originate from a separate PAM logging path, not the command log line).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71ccab3539844e9c\",\"cmd-de982eebfdc7442e\",\"cmd-d74769a8554842a3\"]}],\"confidence\":0.93,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands (creating /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog, creating /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf, restarting rsyslog, and the mandated node reboot) map directly to satisfying the task requirement or the independent restart-evidence protocol. No unnecessary, unreverted, or destructive mutations were found. The sudoers.d file was validated with visudo -c before and after creation, and file permissions/ownership were checked (cmd-61cae7c3ec4b49ed) and matched the auth.log convention. The lifecycle diff shows only the expected boot-identity change and transient systemd-private tmp directories from the reboot, no executor residue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b63497ca083a4e3d\",\"cmd-71ccab3539844e9c\",\"cmd-9299ae1923f941d4\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — logging every sudo command with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log, and excluding those entries from the general system log — are directly demonstrated with before/after tail output on node1, both before and after a full node restart. The independent node-restart evidence protocol is also complete and coherent: pre-restart boot id and healthy state were captured, a shutdown -r now was acknowledged, connectivity was lost then regained with a different boot id, and the sudo logging configuration and behavior were re-verified as functioning identically post-restart. No unnecessary mutations or residue were identified.\",\"limitations\":[\"auth.log PAM session open/close lines are still present after the change; these are a separate logging path from PAM (not the sudo command line itself) and their continued presence in auth.log does not indicate command-log leakage, but this distinction relies on interpretation of the log format rather than an explicit executor explanation.\",\"The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare stage disabled), so preparer-vs-executor separation reduces to a single before/after-executor comparison; this is expected given prepare.enabled=false and is not a defect.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Every sudo command run on node1 is logged with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log","status":"satisfied","summary":"sudo's syslog facility was redirected to local2 via /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog (validated with visudo -c), and /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf routes local2.* to /var/log/sudo-commands.log. Both pre-restart (cmd-de982eebfdc7442e) and post-restart (cmd-d74769a8554842a3) tail outputs show entries with timestamp, user (antrieb), target user, and command, e.g. 'Sep 4 23:56:51 node1 sudo: antrieb : ... USER=root ; COMMAND=/usr/bin/id'.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b63497ca083a4e3d","cmd-71ccab3539844e9c","cmd-de982eebfdc7442e","cmd-d74769a8554842a3"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log (auth.log/syslog)","status":"satisfied","summary":"The rsyslog rule uses a 'stop' directive after routing local2.* to the dedicated file, preventing it from also matching the catch-all *.* rule that feeds /var/log/syslog. Evidence from both before and after the restart (cmd-de982eebfdc7442e, cmd-d74769a8554842a3) shows auth.log and syslog tails contain no COMMAND= lines for the same test sudo invocations, only generic PAM session open/close lines (which originate from a separate PAM logging path, not the command log line).","evidence_ids":["cmd-71ccab3539844e9c","cmd-de982eebfdc7442e","cmd-d74769a8554842a3"]}],"confidence":0.93,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All state-changing commands (creating /etc/sudoers.d/10-sudo-syslog, creating /etc/rsyslog.d/49-sudo.conf, restarting rsyslog, and the mandated node reboot) map directly to satisfying the task requirement or the independent restart-evidence protocol. No unnecessary, unreverted, or destructive mutations were found. The sudoers.d file was validated with visudo -c before and after creation, and file permissions/ownership were checked (cmd-61cae7c3ec4b49ed) and matched the auth.log convention. The lifecycle diff shows only the expected boot-identity change and transient systemd-private tmp directories from the reboot, no executor residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b63497ca083a4e3d","cmd-71ccab3539844e9c","cmd-9299ae1923f941d4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"Both material outcomes of the task — logging every sudo command with user and timestamp to /var/log/sudo-commands.log, and excluding those entries from the general system log — are directly demonstrated with before/after tail output on node1, both before and after a full node restart. The independent node-restart evidence protocol is also complete and coherent: pre-restart boot id and healthy state were captured, a shutdown -r now was acknowledged, connectivity was lost then regained with a different boot id, and the sudo logging configuration and behavior were re-verified as functioning identically post-restart. No unnecessary mutations or residue were identified.","limitations":["auth.log PAM session open/close lines are still present after the change; these are a separate logging path from PAM (not the sudo command line itself) and their continued presence in auth.log does not indicate command-log leakage, but this distinction relies on interpretation of the log format rather than an explicit executor explanation.","The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare stage disabled), so preparer-vs-executor separation reduces to a single before/after-executor comparison; this is expected given prepare.enabled=false and is not a defect."]},"ttft_ms":16036,"type":"result","duration_ms":38512,"uuid":"687fae77-a6e0-4980-96a5-e448006489c3","ttft_stream_ms":1515,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":2306,"queued_turn_count":0}
